## Scope

This draft candidate closes the remaining source-side d6 gaps that can be closed without fabricating live repository, hardware, signing, or runtime evidence:

- deterministic D2I ext4 metadata normalization bound to the committed source epoch (inode/parent-directory/superblock fields), with two-preparation byte equality required;
- exact e2fsprogs repository/commit/tag/version binding in the D2I workflow;
- fail-closed governance command-graph scanning for dynamic Git/GitHub/HTTP forms, wrappers, process substitutions, unquoted heredoc expansions, Python subprocess/HTTP aliases, chained imports, and exec/spawn launchers;
- strict D1 epoch bounds and verifier binding;
- synchronized contracts/docs and regression coverage.

## Exact source identity

- Base `main`: `afd42c0f90d254dfb7b04d9c45216e879840f95e`
