## Local verification

- 323 Python unit tests;
- repository, project-truth, D0T-03, D0C-04, browser/codec, receipt, systemd-custody, and D3 validators;
- Rust 1.93 locked workspace fmt/check/clippy/test, including all-features;
- bash syntax for all tracked shell scripts and the exact D2I ShellCheck 0.10.0 list;
- synthetic D2I preparation twice from the same ext4 base: image and receipt bytes matched.

The exact candidate-head Actions matrix is intentionally reported separately and must be terminal before any promotion claim.

## Claim ceiling / blockers

This remains Draft and `merge_ready=false`. It does not claim protected-main settings, required-check enforcement, organization-team CODEOWNERS, independent approvals, signing-key custody, exact-main promotion, QEMU/Servo/D1/D2I qualification, live cross-UID development activation, or D4-D9 release authority. The source contract explicitly scopes `repository_write=false` to remote/protected source and promotion refs; ephemeral checkout fetches used to bind exact objects are not release authority.

Open external/upstream blockers remain tracked in issues #31, #34, #42, #48, #50, and #51. Historical evidence stays stale until the exact head and later exact-main promotion gates prove otherwise. No self-approval, self-merge, administrator bypass, or auto-merge is permitted.
